```slide boxes
id: a1
title: An assistant's four parts
items:
- heading: Instructions
  text: What it does, in what order, and what it never does
  icon: list-checks
- heading: Knowledge
  text: The files or folder it answers from
  icon: book-open
- heading: Skills
  text: Small skills it can call on
  icon: puzzle
- heading: Tools
  text: What it may open, send or change
  icon: wrench
```

An assistant is set up once and used every day. Its four parts decide what it does well, and what it must never do.

TRY IT

```
You are an assistant for the customer service team. Answer only from the files in the Policies folder. If the answer isn't there, say so and name who to ask.
```

```slide columns
id: a2
title: An assistant, or an agent?
items:
- heading: Assistant
  text: "Answers when you ask\nWorks in the chat\nYou check every step"
- heading: Agent
  text: "Works on a goal by itself\nUses tools and files\nYou check the result"
```

An agent is given a goal, not a question. It picks the steps, uses tools and files, and comes back with a result you check.

